# H6199 effect definition uploaded over 0xA3, captured 2026-08-05 from the Govee Home iOS
# app driving the DreamView T1. Applying a saved Snapshot, which replays a stored device
# state rather than authoring anything: the same apply also sent 33 04 brightness and a
# 33 05 04 scene select, and no register this protocol did not already have. That is the
# whole answer to what a snapshot is on the wire.
#
# Kept because it is the widest scene body captured: three blocks of 44, 32 and 35 bytes,
# where the rest of the corpus runs 26 to 47 in ones and twos. A trailer claimed to sit at
# the block's end has to hold for a 44-byte block too, and this is the fixture that says so.
id: h6199_effect_snapshot_3block
data: h6199_effect_snapshot_3block.bin
imports:
  - h6199_effect_upload
asserts:
  - actual: kind
    expected: 2
  - actual: content.block_count
    expected: 3
  - actual: content.blocks[0].len
    expected: 44
  - actual: content.blocks[1].len
    expected: 32
  - actual: content.blocks[2].len
    expected: 35
